r horror i think  and this stuff drives me crazy in recent  years fantasy has become much more  popular than  science fiction to my mind this is just  cyclical it was just a reverse when i  was breaking in  back in the 70s 60s and 70s science  fiction was much more popular in fantasy  you could hardly find any fantasy these  days fantasy outsells science fiction  someday it'll probably reverse again or  horror will come along we'll sell all of  it more  who the hell knows there are these  trends in that but to my mind it doesn't  matter it's all  imaginative literature and yet you see  some people and it particularly seems to  come from the science fiction side  who really feel that these two things  are antithetical who will  say that oh science fiction is rigorous  and  logical and uh it's precious bodily  fluid should be pure and  fantasy is this mind stuff that'll rot  your mind and all that  i think that argument is tripe i think  these are basically two flavors of  imaginative literature and all that  matters is the furniture  ultimately whether we're writing about  castles or  spaceships or vampires it's still the  human heart in conflict with itself that  matters  and the rest of it is just set dressing  furniture  what have you

